# Cairn identity — a self-sovereign member root and its device tree (v2).
# There is NO household root and no trusted-root set. A member root is its own
# apex: it SELF-signs an identity_attestation carrying its self-asserted profile.
# No private key is ever copied; trust propagates as signed, content-addressed
# objects in the identity log. Edges are labelled by object type.
direction: down

alice: "Member root — Alice (human)\n(offline apex — her own 24 words)\nSELF-signs her identity_attestation" {
  shape: hexagon
  style.fill: "#ecfdf5"
  style.stroke: "#047857"
  style.bold: true
}
agent: "Member root — Assistant (agent)\noperated_by = Alice\n(also self-attests)" {
  shape: hexagon
  style.fill: "#fff7ed"
  style.stroke: "#c2410c"
}

laptop: "Laptop\n(device key)" { style.fill: "#f1f5f9" }
phone: "Phone\n(device key)" { style.fill: "#f1f5f9" }
tablet: "Tablet\n(device key)" { style.fill: "#f1f5f9" }
session: "Session key\n(browser, ~hours)" { style.fill: "#fefce8"; shape: circle }
agentdev: "Agent instance\n(device key)" { style.fill: "#f1f5f9" }

alice -> laptop: "device_delegation\n(first device — signed by member root)" { style.stroke: "#047857" }
laptop -> phone: "device_delegation\n(paired from laptop)" { style.stroke: "#334155" }
phone -> tablet: "device_delegation\n(paired from phone)" { style.stroke: "#334155" }
phone -> session: "session_delegation\n(signed by device / passkey)" { style.stroke: "#a16207" }
agent -> agentdev: "device_delegation" { style.stroke: "#c2410c" }

explain: |md
  **Devices form a tree per member.** The member root signs only the *first* device,
  then goes offline; each later device is paired from an existing one. A verifier
  walks any signing key up to the member root it belongs to.

  **A valid chain proves identity, not trustworthiness.** It says "this key belongs
  to member M, who *claims* this name" — nothing more. Whether to trust M is decided
  at the **edge**: you paired with them, a room you are both in admitted them, or a
  relay you use lists them.
| { near: bottom-center; style.font-size: 13 }
